// title: Hack the ctOS
// xp: 25
// hidden: profile #test(0)["ctOS-00000000"]
// hidden: profile #test(255)["ctOS-000000FF"]
// hint: The id is shown in decimal. ctOS speaks hexadecimal, eight digits of it, in capitals.
// hint: Everything goes in the spec of one hole: the fill, the width and the kind of number. The kind for capital hex digits is a capital letter.
//
// In Chicago one operating system runs everything: traffic lights,
// bridges, your fridge. Every citizen has a ctOS profile, and Aiden Pearce
// wants to read them all. A profile's name is `ctOS-` and its id as eight
// hexadecimal digits, in capitals, with zeros in front.
//
// `profile` gets the prefix right and nothing else. *Hack the planet!*
// (Wrong franchise, same spirit.)
#test(48879)["ctOS-0000BEEF"]
#test(3735928559)["ctOS-DEADBEEF"]
#test(1)["ctOS-00000001"]
fun profile(id: uint32) -> str {
    return f"ctOS-{id}"
}
